4. ace_env_lfo_fx_basic.yaml
text
catalog_version: 1
schema_version: 1

envelopes:
  - id: "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
    version: 1
    status: "active"
    name: "Generic ADSR"
    origin: "OMEGA"
    engine: "VirtualAnalog"
    family: "Envelope"
    model_id: "GenericAdsr"
    type: "ADSR"
    tags: [ "env", "generic" ]
    parameters:
      - name: "attack"
        label: "Attack"
        unit: "ms"
        min: 0.1
        max: 10000.0
        default: 10.0
      - name: "decay"
        label: "Decay"
        unit: "ms"
        min: 0.1
        max: 10000.0
        default: 120.0
      - name: "sustain"
        label: "Sustain"
        unit: "normalized"
        min: 0.0
        max: 1.0
        default: 0.7
      - name: "release"
        label: "Release"
        unit: "ms"
        min: 0.1
        max: 10000.0
        default: 300.0
    modulation_targets: [ ]

lfos:
  - id: "LFO-001"
    version: 1
    status: "active"
    name: "Generic LFO"
    origin: "OMEGA (Juno-style)"
    engine: "VirtualAnalog"
    family: "LFO"
    model_id: "GenericLfo"
    tags: [ "lfo", "generic" ]
    parameters:
      - name: "rate"
        label: "Rate"
        unit: "Hz"
        min: 0.01
        max: 20.0
        default: 0.5
      - name: "shape"
        label: "Shape"
        unit: "enum"
        enum_values: [ "sine", "triangle", "saw", "square", "random" ]
        default: "triangle"
      - name: "delay"
        label: "Delay"
        unit: "ms"
        min: 0.0
        max: 10000.0
        default: 0.0
    modulation_targets: [ ]   # el LFO es fuente, no destino

fx:
  - id: "FX-CH-001"
    version: 1
    status: "active"
    name: "Juno BBD Chorus"
    origin: "Roland Juno-106"
    engine: "FX"
    family: "Chorus"
    model_id: "RolandJunoChorus"
    tags: [ "chorus", "bbd", "juno", "stereo" ]
    parameters:
      - name: "mix"
        label: "Mix"
        unit: "normalized"
        min: 0.0
        max: 1.0
        default: 0.7
      - name: "mode"
        label: "Mode"
        unit: "enum"
        enum_values: [ "I", "II", "I+II" ]
        default: "I+II"
    modulation_targets:
      - id: "mix"
        label: "Mix"
        unit: "normalized"

  # FX genérico para fallback
  - id: "FX-CH-GENERIC"
    version: 1
    status: "active"
    name: "Generic Chorus"
    origin: "OMEGA"
    engine: "FX"
    family: "Chorus"
    model_id: "GenericChorus"
    tags: [ "chorus", "generic" ]
    parameters:
      - name: "mix"
        label: "Mix"
        unit: "normalized"
        min: 0.0
        max: 1.0
        default: 0.5
    modulation_targets:
      - id: "mix"
        label: "Mix"
        unit: "normalized"
Con estos tres ficheros ya puedes:

Implementar AceCatalog::createFromResources() leyendo ace_index.yaml y los otros.

Usar getComponent(id) en AceValidator y en el Binding.

Construir presets como el “Hybrid MS20 + JP Supersaw Pad” usando estos ids.





Para que todo encaje con JUCE, te propongo este esquema de ValueTree de preset, alineado con ACE y EngineConfig.

1. Árbol raíz del preset
text
OMEGA_PRESET
 ├─ Global
 ├─ Layers
 │   ├─ LayerA
 │   └─ LayerB
 └─ Metadata
Claves principales:

OMEGA_PRESET (type): nodo raíz del estado.

Props en raíz:

engine (p.ej. "VirtualAnalog")

catalogVersion (int, opcional)

2. Nodo Global
Parámetros macro (espejo de APVTS, si quieres):

text
Global
 ├─ (props)
Props típicas:

masterGain

macro1..macroN

layerMixA, layerMixB (si lo quieres también aquí)

Estos parámetros también existen como parámetros APVTS; el ValueTree es solo su copia serializada.
​

3. Nodo Layers
text
Layers
 ├─ LayerA
 └─ LayerB
Cada LayerX tiene esta estructura:

text
LayerA
 ├─ VoiceArchitecture
 ├─ Modulation
 └─ LayerParams
Props en LayerA:

id = "A"

name = "MS20 Grit"

polyphony (int)

engine (de la layer, normalmente igual a global)

3.1 VoiceArchitecture (JUCE)
text
VoiceArchitecture
 ├─ Oscillators
 ├─ Filters
 ├─ Envelopes
 ├─ Lfos
 └─ Fx
Oscillators
text
Oscillators
 ├─ Osc1
 └─ Osc2
Osc1 props:

slot (int)

componentId = "OSC-VA-002" (ACE id)

enabled (bool)

Parámetros propios (mismas claves que en ACE):

tune

shape

fm_amount

…

Idem para Osc2 con su componentId (por ejemplo, "OSC-VA-001").
​

Filters
text
Filters
 └─ Filter1
Filter1 props:

slot (int)

componentId = "FLT-VA-003"

enabled (bool)

mode = "HP+LP Series"

Parámetros: cutoff, resonance, drive…

Envelopes
text
Envelopes
 ├─ Env1
 └─ Env2
Props:

slot (int)

componentId = "ENV-ADSR-GEN"

role = "amp" / "filter"

Parámetros: attack, decay, sustain, release…
​

LFOs
text
Lfos
 └─ Lfo1
Props:

slot (int)

componentId = "LFO-001"

rate, shape, delay…
​

FX
text
Fx
 └─ Fx1
Props:

slot (int)

componentId = "FX-CH-001"

enabled (bool)

Parámetros: mix, mode…
​

3.2 Modulation
text
Modulation
 ├─ LocalRoutes
 └─ GlobalRoutes
LocalRoutes
text
LocalRoutes
 ├─ Route0
 ├─ Route1
 └─ ...
RouteN props:

source = "ENV2", "LFO1", "KeyTrack", etc.

destination = "LayerA.Filter1.cutoff" (cadena según convención)
​

amount (float)

curve (string: "linear", "exponential", "s-curve"…)

bipolar (bool opcional)

GlobalRoutes
Rutas que usan fuentes globales (ModWheel, Aftertouch…) hacia la layer:

text
GlobalRoutes
 └─ Route0 (ej. source="ModWheel", destination="LayerA.Filter1.cutoff", ...)
3.3 LayerParams
text
LayerParams
 └─ (props)
Props típicas:

levelDb (ganancia de la layer)

pan

mute / solo

Estos pueden mapearse a parámetros APVTS si quieres (por ejemplo, LAYER_A_LEVEL, LAYER_A_PAN).

4. Nodo Metadata
text
Metadata
 └─ (props)
Props:

name

author

tags (quizá como string CSV o child nodes)

bpm, key

createdAt, updatedAt, etc.
​

5. Cómo encaja con ACE y Validator
AceCatalog solo se preocupa de componentId y de los nombres de parámetros/targets que aparecen bajo cada OscX/FilterX/etc.

AceValidator recorre:

Layers/Layer*/VoiceArchitecture → valida componentId, rellena defaults, aplica fallbacks.

Modulation → valida source y destination contra la arquitectura y ACE.
​

VoiceFactory usa VoiceArchitecture validado para construir VoiceArchitectureRuntime.
​

ModulationGraph usa Modulation validado para construir ModulationRoutingRuntime.
​

Todo esto ocurre fuera del audio thread; el engine solo ve los runtimes resultantes.
​

Con este esquema ya puedes:

Serializar/deserializar presets OMEGA ↔ ValueTree de JUCE de forma directa.
​

Te dejo la traducción 1:1 del preset híbrido al esquema de ValueTree que acabamos de definir. Es pseudocódigo de estructura, no C++, para que veas tipos y keys.

1. Raíz y nodos principales
text
ValueTree type: "OMEGA_PRESET"
  properties:
    engine = "VirtualAnalog"
    catalogVersion = 1
Hijos:

text
OMEGA_PRESET
 ├─ Global        (type: "Global")
 ├─ Layers        (type: "Layers")
 └─ Metadata      (type: "Metadata")
2. Nodo Global
text
Global (type: "Global")
  properties:
    masterGain = 0.0          // dB
    macro1 = 0.0
    macro2 = 0.0
    // etc, los que quieras
3. Nodo Layers
text
Layers (type: "Layers")
  children:
    LayerA (type: "Layer")
    LayerB (type: "Layer")
3.1 LayerA
text
LayerA (type: "Layer")
  properties:
    id = "A"
    name = "MS20 Grit"
    polyphony = 8
    engine = "VirtualAnalog"

  children:
    VoiceArchitecture (type: "VoiceArchitecture")
    Modulation        (type: "Modulation")
    LayerParams       (type: "LayerParams")
3.1.1 LayerA.VoiceArchitecture
text
VoiceArchitecture (type: "VoiceArchitecture")
  children:
    Oscillators (type: "Oscillators")
    Filters     (type: "Filters")
    Envelopes   (type: "Envelopes")
    Lfos        (type: "Lfos")
    Fx          (type: "Fx")
Osciladores:

text
Oscillators
  ├─ Osc1 (type: "Oscillator")
  └─ Osc2 (type: "Oscillator")
Osc1 (MS‑20 VCO):

text
Osc1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "OSC-VA-002"     // Korg VCO
    enabled = true
    tune = 0.0
    shape = 0                       // saw
    fm_amount = 0.0
Osc2 (Juno DCO sub‑refuerzo):

text
Osc2
  properties:
    slot = 2
    componentId = "OSC-VA-001"     // Juno DCO
    enabled = true
    tune = -12.0
    pulse_width = 0.5
    sub_level = 0.5
Filtro:

text
Filters
  └─ Filter1 (type: "Filter")
Filter1 (KORG35 MS‑20):

text
Filter1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "FLT-VA-003"     // KORG35
    enabled = true
    mode = "HP+LP Series"
    cutoff = 800.0
    resonance = 0.6
    drive = 3.0
Envolventes:

text
Envelopes
  ├─ Env1 (type: "Envelope")
  └─ Env2 (type: "Envelope")
Env1 (amp):

text
Env1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
    role = "amp"
    attack = 10.0
    decay = 120.0
    sustain = 0.7
    release = 300.0
Env2 (filter):

text
Env2
  properties:
    slot = 2
    componentId = "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
    role = "filter"
    attack = 5.0
    decay = 200.0
    sustain = 0.3
    release = 250.0
LFO:

text
Lfos
  └─ Lfo1 (type: "Lfo")
Lfo1:

text
Lfo1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "LFO-001"
    rate = 0.4
    shape = "triangle"
    delay = 0.0
FX:

text
Fx
  └─ Fx1 (type: "Fx")
Fx1 (chorus Juno):

text
Fx1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "FX-CH-001"
    enabled = true
    mix = 0.4
    mode = "I+II"
3.1.2 LayerA.Modulation
text
Modulation
  children:
    LocalRoutes  (type: "LocalRoutes")
    GlobalRoutes (type: "GlobalRoutes")
LocalRoutes:

text
LocalRoutes
  ├─ Route0 (type: "Route")
  └─ Route1 (type: "Route")
Route0 (ENV2 → cutoff):

text
Route0
  properties:
    source = "ENV2"
    destination = "LayerA.Filter1.cutoff"
    amount = 0.5
    curve = "exponential"
    bipolar = false
Route1 (LFO1 → pitch osc1):

text
Route1
  properties:
    source = "LFO1"
    destination = "LayerA.Osc1.pitch"
    amount = 0.1
    curve = "sine"
    bipolar = true
GlobalRoutes (ejemplo vacío por ahora):

text
GlobalRoutes
  // sin rutas en este preset
3.1.3 LayerA.LayerParams
text
LayerParams
  properties:
    levelDb = -3.0
    pan = -0.1
    mute = false
3.2 LayerB (JP Supersaw Pad)
Misma estructura:

text
LayerB (type: "Layer")
  properties:
    id = "B"
    name = "JP Supersaw Pad"
    polyphony = 8
    engine = "VirtualAnalog"

  children:
    VoiceArchitecture
    Modulation
    LayerParams
LayerB.VoiceArchitecture:

Osciladores:

text
Oscillators
  ├─ Osc1
  └─ Osc2
Osc1 (supersaw):

text
Osc1
  properties:
    slot = 1
    componentId = "OSC-VA-004"
    enabled = true
    detune = 0.4
    spread = 0.6
    brightness = 0.5
Osc2 (Juno DCO):

text
